sec.p:
For a given formulation (assuming Newtonian behavior), injectability at a predetermined speed is governed by factors such as needle gauge and surface area of the syringe plunger. Pressure generated within the syringe barrel (P) during injection is directly proportional to the force (F) exerted on the back of the syringe plunger and inversely proportional to surface area of the syringe plunger (A) (Eq. 1). Therefore, in the case of certain high-viscosity formulations, one approach to reduce injection forces could entail the use of syringes with reduced barrel diameter which corresponds to lower surface area of the syringe plunger.1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
